{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.WritheMarkovInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.WritheMarkovInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.coulombCharge_not_stabilization_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.coulombCharge_not_stabilization_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L199-L211","doc":"**The Coulomb charge is not stabilisation-invariant.**\n\n`Q = w/2` shifts by `1/2` under a move that does not change the link.  So `Q`\nis a function of the braid word (or of a canonical normal form), not of the\nlink — contrary to `sm-lagrangian-selection-rules.md`'s claim that it is\nconstant on gauge orbits, given that the same corpus says vertical moves are\npart of the gauge freedom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_stabilize_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_stabilize_neg","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L190-L197","doc":"Negative stabilisation shifts it by `-1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_stabilize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_stabilize","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L180-L188","doc":"**Stabilisation shifts the writhe by `+1`.**\n\n`β ↦ βσ_n` presents the *same link* but adds one positive crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_conj","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L169-L176","doc":"**Conjugation preserves the writhe.**\n\nThe horizontal / fixed-`n` direction of the gauge groupoid leaves the writhe\nalone, so `Q = w/2` and `I₃` *are* invariant under it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_inv","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L160-L165","doc":"The writhe of the inverse word is the negation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_neg_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_neg_map","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L148-L158","doc":"Negating every letter negates the writhe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe_append","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L142-L146","doc":"The writhe is additive under concatenation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.inv","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L123-L124","doc":"The inverse braid word: reverse the letters and invert each generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.writhe","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L120-L121","doc":"The writhe: the sum of the crossing signs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.BraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.MarkovInvariance.BraidWord","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/WritheMarkovInvariance.lean#L116-L118","doc":"A braid word: entry `±i` denotes `σᵢ^{±1}`.  Same convention as\n`ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean`; restated here so this file stands alone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}